   "text": "1Three teaspoons sugar (15g) in 1 cup (200mL) water. 2If dextrose 10% unavailable: mix 1 part dextrose 50% to 4 parts water for injection to make dextrose 10% solution. 3If dextrose 5% not available: add 10mL dextrose 50% to each 100mL of sodium chloride 0.9%. 4 BMI = weight (kg) ÷ height (m) ÷ height (m). 5Polycystic ovarian syndrome to change to polyendocrine metabolic ovarian syndrome. 6Cardiovascular disease (CVD) includes ischaemic heart disease, peripheral vascular disease and stroke/ TIA. 7 Thirst, dry mouth, poor skin turgor, BP < 90/60, pulse ≥ 100. 8Unexplained weight loss, tiredness, thirst (especially at night), passing excessive amounts of urine often, periodic changes in vision, frequent infections (e.g. urinary, skin). 9If shock/SBP <80, also give 20mL/kg bolus and repeat until SBP > 80. Avoid giving > 50mL/kg in the first 4 hours. 10Avoid using insulin needle, use 22-25 gauge needle.",
